<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Greensleeves-Am-Theme" spTempo="108">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1580 (first documented registration;
	the tune may be older)
Composer:	Traditional — anonymous
Lyricist:	Traditional — anonymous
Form:	16-bar verse-and-refrain structure,
	with repeated harmonic patterns
Style:	English folk song / Renaissance
Key:	A minor (common modern version)

“Greensleeves” was registered in London in
September 1580 under the title “A Newe Northen
Dittye of ye Ladye Greene Sleves.” It was once
popularly attributed to Henry VIII, but that claim is
historically unlikely because the song’s Italianate
musical style appears to have reached England
after Henry’s death; the original composer and
lyricist remain unknown.</spComments>
